"into the two edge windows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:112
msgid ""
"``mapping`` assigns each sampled name to a ``len_args`` key. A target can"
" also be written explicitly as ``len_args.R`` or "
"``other_args.some_name``. Fixed values remain in the template, so only "
"parameters that actually vary need to appear in ``sampling``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:118
msgid "Scanning radial configurations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:120
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"``sampling.mode: grid`` forms the Cartesian product of all sampled "
"arrays. ``paired`` zips arrays of the same length and broadcasts scalar "
"entries. For example, this scans :math:`r_{13}` while holding "
":math:`r_{12}` and both shell widths fixed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:151
msgid ""
"The result has one row per expanded sample and one column per multipole "
"order. The original sampled values are stored in ``sample_params`` so "
"rows remain self-describing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:155
msgid "3PCF monopole for thin and finite-width radial shells"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:160
msgid ""
"A broader radial bin averages neighbouring triangle configurations and "
"suppresses small-scale fluctuations without changing the task structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:164
msgid "Parallel execution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:166
msgid "The task separates two kinds of parallel work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:168
msgid "``serial``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:169
msgid ""
"One rank evaluates all samples and multipole modes. Use this for a small "
"local check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:172
msgid "``pair_mpi``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:173
msgid ""
"MPI-rank pairs share the :math:`(\\ell,m)` convolution work for one "
"sample. It requires an even number of ranks and is well suited to one or "
"a few configurations with many multipoles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:177
msgid "``sample_mpi``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:178
msgid ""
"Samples are assigned to ranks by static round robin. It is the natural "
"mode for a long monopole or radial-window scan. The current "
"implementation uses ``sample_mpi.ranks_per_sample: 1``; choose "
"approximately one rank per simultaneous sample, then use ``threads`` for "
"the local FFT and kernel work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:183
msgid ""
"In ``sample_mpi``, rank 0 reads each file-backed ``SFCField`` once and "
"broadcasts it. This avoids every rank independently stressing shared "
"storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:187
msgid "CPU and GPU backends"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:189
msgid "``summation_backend`` controls the final contraction and grid sum:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:191
msgid "``cpu`` uses the multithreaded CPU kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:192
msgid ""
"``gpu`` transfers the filtered fields to the selected CUDA device and "
"uses ``gpu_threads_per_block`` for the final contraction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:195
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The preceding FFT convolution stage remains CPU/MPI work in both cases. "
"Thus a GPU changes the contraction backend, not the estimator, radial "
"windows, or input fields. At high :math:`\\ell_{\\max}` the GPU path is "
"usually most useful; for a short monopole scan, sample-level CPU "
"parallelism may be simpler and competitive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:201
msgid ""
"The current CPU/GPU timing, numerical-agreement, and host-memory "
"comparison is kept in one place on :doc:`../../benchmark`.  The saved "
"multipoles agree to relative :math:`L_2` differences below ``2.3e-14``; "
"only the contraction backend changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:207
msgid "Products and output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:209
msgid ""
"Available products are ``ddd_l``, ``rrr_l``, ``delta_ddd_l``, and "
"``zeta_l``. Requesting ``zeta_l`` expands the connected-data and random "
"dependencies automatically. A fully uniform random field uses an analytic"
" monopole-only ``rrr_l`` shortcut."
msgstr ""

#: ../../get_start/corr_3pcf_multipole/corr_3pcf_multipole.rst:223
msgid ""
"``zeta_condition`` records the conditioning of the random-multipole "
"solve. Inspect unusually large values before interpreting a noisy high-"
"order result."
msgstr ""

